{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>The ark.</b> Scripture begins with the most select of the vessels, just as it began with the Mishkan by starting with the linen curtains, which are the supreme boundary of holiness in the House. And its saying <b>and its poles</b> — Scripture informs us that the poles are equal to the body of the ark in holiness, and therefore you will find that Scripture commanded (Exodus 25:15): ״לֹא יָסוּרוּ מִמֶּנּוּ״. And its saying <b>the cover</b> — it is not equal to the holiness of the ark, and likewise you will find that it was not fixed to the ark, nor is there any warning against removing it. And its saying <b>and the parokhet of the screen</b> — Scripture has placed its holiness on a par with the holiness of the cover, for they are in one category."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:46.919608905Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}